  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SURVEYING THE CRITICALLY ENDANGERED PANCAKE TORTOISE ON THREE PROTECTED WILDLIFE CONSERVANCIES IN KENYA TO ESTABLISH POPULATION RANGE EXTENSION AND DEVELOP LONG-TERM CONSERVATION STRATEGY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT CONSERVATION ACTIVITIES TO PROTECT THE PANCAKE TORTOISE FROM POACHING FOR THE PET TRADE AND DESTRUCTION OF ITS ROCK HABITAT. NATIVE ONLY TO KENYA AND TANZANIA, POPULATIONS OF THIS TORTOISE ARE DECREASING WIDELY THROUGHOUT ITS RANGE. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE:(1)CONDUCTING POPULATION SURVEYS TO ASSESS ITS POPULATION STATUS WITHIN THE LEWA-BORANA LANDSCAPE WHICH INCLUDES THREE PROTECTED AREAS (2) COLLECTING GENETIC SAMPLES TO DETERMINE POPULATION DIVERSITY (3) PREPARING A LANDSCAPE-SCALE CONSERVATION MANAGEMENT PLAN AND (4) ANALYZING AND SHARING RECOMMENDATIONS AND CONSERVATION PLANS WITH NEARBY CONSERVANCIES AND PRIVATE RANCHES.</narrative>
  </description>
